<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113067" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὁ</span>: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκεῖς,</span>
		
			Att.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					490
				</span></i>
			 (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				370d
			</span></i>, 
				Ep.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῆες</span> (v. infr.): acc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκέας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					221e
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				428d
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκεῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.214a
				</span></i>
			:—<i>coppersmith,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκτων</span> (joiner, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				370d
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἣν [ἀσπίδα] χ. ἤλασεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.295
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίτρη, τὴν χαλκῆες κάμον ἄνδρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.187
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				216
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>worker in metal,</i> of a <i>goldsmith,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.432
			</span></i>; of a <i>worker in iron.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				9.391
			</span></i>; hence later, <i>blacksmith, smith</i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκέας τοὺς τὸν σίδηρον ἐργαζομένους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Po.</u>
					1461a29
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.68
			</span></i>, Ar.l.c., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				3.4.17
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.200
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. χαλκοῦ καὶ σιδήρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ge.</u>
					4.22
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>John Dory, Zeus faber,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				1.133
			</span></i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				535b18
			</span></i>; distd. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκίς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.328d
			</span></i>.</div>
